// A pointer, not a config. Every basedpyright setting lives in
// backend/pyproject.toml next to ruff's and pytest's; this file exists only so the
// editor can find them.
//
// A language server searches its worktree root for a config and does not descend into
// subdirectories, so it never sees backend/pyproject.toml. That matters more than it
// sounds: basedpyright ignores a developer's personal typeCheckingMode ONLY when it
// finds a project config. Finding none, it applies the editor's own settings instead -
// so anyone whose global Zed or VS Code config sets a mode got that rather than this
// repo's "strict", and no editor configuration could reconcile the two.
//
// "extends" accepts a .json or a .toml, and relative paths inside the extended file
// resolve against that file's own location - which is why include = ["src", "tests"]
// in backend/pyproject.toml means backend/src and backend/tests, not the repo root.
//
// Do not add settings here. Anything in this file would override the values it points
// at, which is exactly the split-brain this arrangement exists to prevent.
{
  "extends": "backend/pyproject.toml"
}
